  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PSS Protection and Psychosocial Support for Children in Conflict &#x2013; Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">750 children aged from 6-15 years will be benefited from the project (Palestinian refugees from Lebanon, displaced Palestinian refugees from Syria; 60% females and 40% males) in total. The percentage of PWD is 2+%. Besides, around 150 parents will benefit from project services (raising awareness, 15group and individual therapy). Activities: o 350 children from 6 to 15 years old enrolled in the center&#x2019;s PSS program, of those: v 50 children will benefit from individual psychological counselling and support services by the center&#x2019;s psychologist; v 40 children divided in 4 groups will benefit from group psychological counselling and support services by the center&#x2019;s social worker; o 200 Students from 6 to 15 years old targeted with PSS tailored activities inside their 5 elementary and preparatory UNRWA schools in the camp: 40 students per school o 200 Children aged 3 to 15 years old beneficiaries of other organizations in the camp or\and siblings of the children enrolled in Najdeh&#x2019;s PSS program targeted by the center&#x2019;s 10 days summer activities, in addition to the 200 children from the PSS 350 children; o 150 Parents out of 230 family of the 350 children will benefit from the program&#x2019;s curricular activities directed to parents</narrative>
  </description>
